# Rectangular attribute changes: DECCARA and DECRARA, and DECSACE, which says whether they reach
# the stream of cells from the first corner to the second (the default) or the rectangle.
#
# The cases run on a five by three screen of letters. The area is as in rect.vtt.

test DECCARA in rectangle extent changes the rectangle
spec VT510 DECCARA: CSI Pt ; Pl ; Pb ; Pr ; Ps1 ; ... ; Psn $ r changes the attributes in the rectangle; DECSACE 2: all the character positions in the rectangular area
known-fail: alacritty – no DECCARA, DECRARA or DECSACE: they are ignored
size 5 3
feed abcde\r\nfghij\r\nklmno\e[H\e[2*x\e[1;2;2;3;1$r
cell 1,1 attrs=none
cell 1,2 attrs=bold
cell 1,3 attrs=bold
cell 1,4 attrs=none
cell 1,5 attrs=none
cell 2,1 attrs=none
cell 2,2 attrs=bold
cell 2,3 attrs=bold
cell 2,4 attrs=none
cell 2,5 attrs=none
cell 3,2 attrs=none
row 1 |abcde|
row 2 |fghij|
test DECCARA setting an attribute that cells have already leaves it set
spec VT510 DECCARA: Ps1 = 1 sets bold in the rectangle, whatever it was before
known-fail: alacritty – no DECCARA, DECRARA or DECSACE: they are ignored
size 5 3
feed \e[1mabc\e[0mde\e[H\e[2*x\e[1;1;1;5;1$r
cell 1,1 attrs=bold
cell 1,3 attrs=bold
cell 1,4 attrs=bold
cell 1,5 attrs=bold
